  "summary": "Eternal Darkness: Sanity’s Requiem is a GameCube horror adventure that follows different people through a story spanning two millennia. Silicon Knights uses changing periods and locations to give an ancient struggle a human scale. Each chapter offers another perspective, with weapons and surroundings appropriate to its protagonist. Exploration, combat and rune-based magic connect these episodes. Alongside the danger inside the fiction, the game develops another source of unease: the possibility that the screen and interface themselves can no longer be completely trusted.",
  "body": [
    "Eternal Darkness: Sanity’s Requiem is a GameCube horror adventure that follows different people through a story spanning two millennia. Silicon Knights uses changing periods and locations to give an ancient struggle a human scale. Each chapter offers another perspective, with weapons and surroundings appropriate to its protagonist. Exploration, combat and rune-based magic connect these episodes. Alongside the danger inside the fiction, the game develops another source of unease: the possibility that the screen and interface themselves can no longer be completely trusted.",
    "The sanity meter falls when a character is seen by certain enemies. As it declines, the game introduces effects that disturb perception: a room may appear wrong, voices may intrude or an apparent technical problem may interrupt play. These moments turn the player’s familiarity with games into something the horror can exploit. Restoring sanity becomes a practical concern, supported by finishing enemies and using appropriate resources. The system gives being observed a consequence that reaches beyond the damage an enemy can inflict.",
    "Combat allows attacks on individual body parts, making the choice of target useful. Removing an enemy’s head changes how it can pursue the protagonist, while the available weapons vary with the historical setting. Magic offers another set of solutions through combinations of runes. It can support fighting and recovery or help reveal a way through an obstruction. These deliberate actions balance the more unpredictable sanity effects: the player must still read the room, choose a method and manage resources while the presentation encourages doubt."
  ],
  "story_headings": [
    "Horror across centuries",
    "When sanity gives way",
    "A body, a weapon, a rune"
  ],
